% c040 (cyclic lens; Adler ch. 1, PDF 19: timbre clarifies form and content; ch. 15, PDF 188-189: at-pitch doubling with an instrument of affinity): 273-276 the violas no longer
% move E4 -> E flat 4 (movement II bar 2's undoing of the thread, at the same pitch, after the thread closed in the violas at 219-220). Upper violas take the
% chain G4-F sharp4-F4-E4 with Hn 1-2 and Tpt 3, so the chain's 3 lands on E4, the violas' E of movement I bar 182 and finale 220; lower violas take C-A-A flat-G (A3-A flat3-G3) with Tbn 1.
% Every chord keeps its pitch classes (E flat at 273 stays in Hn 4 and Bn 1).
